            <ArticleTitle>Transient neurologic symptoms after epidural analgesia in a five-year-old child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>856-7, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transient neurologic symptoms occurred in a five-year-old child after discontinuation of epidural analgesia with bupivacaine and morphine, which had been established for two days after thoracotomy. The symptoms resolved within 12 hours with acetaminophen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
